2010 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Technique Highlight 2\072 Risk vs Reward Path Design\050\050My Method\072 Throughout the level\054 optional paths offer tangible rewards \024 better weapons\054 tactical information \024 but require more time\054 risk\054 or skill to access\056\050\050How I Executed It\072 In Beat 3\054 one landing path gives a silenced weapon enabling stealth but offers no progression\056 The other gives progression but no reward\056 In Beat 4\054 a dark room requires the player to navigate without light in exchange for a sniper rifle\056 In Beat 5\054 security monitors reward curious players with advance knowledge of escape routes\056\050\050Level Example\072 The silenced pistol vs progression split in Beat 3 is the clearest expression of this \024 the player chooses their playstyle through a single spatial decision\056\050)
     /K [ 35 ]
     /P 2011 0 R
     /Pg 1940 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

